# prototype-phase folders (production code lives in src/app/)
# These are anchored with a leading `/` on purpose. An unanchored `prompts/`
# matches a directory named `prompts` at ANY depth, so it also swallowed
# src/app/prompts/ -- which is production code. The files stayed git-tracked
# (gitignore never affects tracked files) so `git ls-files` looked healthy,
# but hatchling honours .gitignore when building the wheel, so app/prompts
# was silently omitted from the package. Local tests and the docker build
# both passed because neither imports the installed wheel; production
# crashed with ModuleNotFoundError on first boot.
prototype/
notebooks/
/prompts

# _markdown/
_nextjs_repo_context/

# interview prep notes
interview_answers_*.md